# Workspace plugin bootstrap resilience

Portal catalog registration must survive **per-workspace plugin load failures** without crashing the host shell.

## Problem (pre-refactor)

`@app-tour/workspace-plugin-host/register` executed `ensureWorkspacePluginsRegistered()` at **module import** time. Codegen registrars statically imported all trunk workspace packages; one broken package prevented portal boot.

## Target model

| Rule | Enforcement |
| ---- | ----------- |
| No side effects on `import` | `register.ts` exports functions only |
| Per-plugin isolation | `registerWorkspacePluginSafe(pluginId)` wraps dynamic `import()` in try/catch |
| Idempotent registration | SDK registries (`registerWorkspaceIntakePlugin`, etc.) tolerate repeat calls |
| `catalogIntake` skip | Workspaces without `catalogIntake` on `WorkspacePlugin` omit intake registration |
| Degraded boot | Portal layout registers **active** `pluginId` only; instrumentation **does not** warm-all by default (P4.4); opt-in `PORTAL_WARM_ALL_PLUGINS=1` |

## Codegen outputs

| File | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| `register-{id}.generated.ts` | Async registrar for one workspace: `registerWorkspaceIntake*` (plugin entry only) + `registerWorkspacePlugin*` (full flow) |
| `workspace-plugin-register-manifest.generated.ts` | `invokeWorkspacePluginRegister` + `invokeWorkspaceIntakeRegister` |

Legacy monolithic `workspace-*-plugins.generated.ts` files are **removed** (P3.1.b). Runtime uses `register-{id}.generated.ts` + `register-safe`.

### Portal wiring (P3.1.a)

| Surface | Call |
| ------- | ---- |
| `apps/portal/instrumentation.ts` | Binds invokers; warm-all only when `PORTAL_WARM_ALL_PLUGINS=1` (P4.4) |
| `apps/portal/app/layout.tsx` | `await registerWorkspacePluginSafe(bootstrap.pluginId)` |
| register page | `await registerWorkspacePluginSafe(workspace)` |
| intake API route | `await registerWorkspaceIntakeSafe(pluginId)` |


## Portal wiring

```text
instrumentation.ts → bind registrars; optional registerAllWorkspacePluginsSafe() if PORTAL_WARM_ALL_PLUGINS=1
register page      → await registerWorkspacePluginSafe(workspace)  // full flow
intake API route   → await registerWorkspaceIntakeSafe(pluginId)   // plugin entry only
```

## Status API

`registerWorkspacePluginSafe` returns `{ status: "ready" | "failed" | "pending", pluginId, error? }` and never throws.

`listHealthyWorkspacePluginIds()` returns plugin ids whose full registration completed with `ready`.

## Telemetry

Per-plugin terminal states emit `workspacePluginBootstrapStatus` events via `setWorkspacePluginBootstrapTelemetrySink` (mirrors `workspace-registry-telemetry.ts`):

```typescript
import {
  setWorkspacePluginBootstrapTelemetrySink,
  type WorkspacePluginBootstrapTelemetryEvent,
} from "@app-tour/workspace-plugin-host";

setWorkspacePluginBootstrapTelemetrySink((event: WorkspacePluginBootstrapTelemetryEvent) => {
  // forward to metrics / tracing — event.kind === "workspacePluginBootstrapStatus"
});
```

Failed loads use code `WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_LOAD_FAILED`; unknown plugin ids use `WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_REGISTER_UNKNOWN`.

## Host package dependencies (P3.2.b)

`@app-tour/workspace-plugin-host` depends only on `@app-tour/workspace-sdk` (contracts). Per-plugin registrars live under `packages/guest-workspace-runtime/src/register-*.generated.ts` (P5.3) and are bound via `setWorkspacePluginRegisterInvokers` / `bindWorkspacePluginRegisterInvokers()` from `@app-tour/guest-workspace-runtime/bind-register-invokers`.

| Layer | Owns |
| ----- | ---- |
| Host | `register-safe`, registration-flow step registry, plugin id revision list |
| Portal | product `import()` registrars + invoker binding |

## Admin web loaders (P4.1 / I3)

`apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-plugin-loaders.generated.ts` is **async-only**: `loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry(pluginId)` uses allowlisted `await import()` + I2 cache. There is no `SYNC_WORKSPACE_PLUGINS` map. Client hydrate uses theme shells in `resolve-bootstrap-workspace-plugin.client.ts` and must not import the generated loaders module.

## Portal package.json product deps (P4.3 → P5.3)

Portal and marketing depend on `@app-tour/guest-workspace-runtime` (not individual product workspace packages). That package declares product deps and owns allowlisted `import("@app-tour/workspace-…")` for registrars, guest theme loaders, and marketing catalog bindings — enforced by `guard-guest-consumer-deps`. Layout still registers one `pluginId`. **P4-D1 closed** in P5.3.a+b.

Architecture depcruise workspace dirs for web/API are **manifest-generated** (`manifest-boundary-allowlist.generated.cjs`, P5.2 / P5.2.b). Host package.json must not list workspace product packages (`guard-guest-frozen-shell`, P5.4).

## Portal instrumentation warm (P4.4)

Default: bind registrars only. Warm-all via `registerAllWorkspacePluginsSafe()` only when `PORTAL_WARM_ALL_PLUGINS` is `1` / `true` / `yes` (non-fatal try/catch).

## Phase 4 metrics (P4.5)

Product trunk **N = 6**. Web/API generated loaders evaluate with **zero** product package static imports; each `load*(pluginId)` touches **one** allowlisted package. Portal instrumentation default touches **zero** products (layout registers active `pluginId` only). See `TEMP/phases/P4-dynamic-workspace-loading-plan.md` §P4.5.
